    "checks": [
      "An accessory apartment is allowed by right (zoning permit) only inside an existing single-family detached house in the MDR and MHDR districts. It is not listed in RR or LDR, whose use lists say 'Only the following uses are permitted' (275-38, 275-46B(6), 275-54B(6))",
      "The house as it stands must have at least 1,500 sq ft, and the main unit must keep at least 900 sq ft (275-190D(1)(c))",
      "One of the units must be owner-occupied for at least 12 months after the conversion (275-190D(1)(b))",
      "The conversion rules of 275-189A(24) apply: the lot must meet the district lot area, yard, building area and parking rules, all work stays inside the existing shell, no second front entrance and no outside stair or fire escape on the front or a street-facing side wall. Extending the sides or raising the height is not a conversion",
      "Parking: two spaces for each dwelling unit, outside the required front yard and to the side or rear of the house (275-142, 275-190D(1)(d), 275-189A(24)(i))",
      "A detached unit, a garage unit and an addition are not listed",
      "Lot area: whether the apartment needs a second share of the district lot area is not settled. MHDR states its single-family lot area per dwelling unit (275-58A)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Bethlehem Township (bethlehemtwp.com). Read on eCode360 in a browser, one section print view at a time. Use lists read for RR, LDR (by right and special exception), MDR and MHDR, and the Neighborhood Enhancement Overlay. AG, NC, GC, PC, OB, GI, LI, CR, Town Center, Mixed-Use Village and Hospital Health Care Village were not opened. The definitions page showed no 'accessory apartment' definition."
  },
